  "listen": "Good morning. This is The Daily Brief for Sunday, October 18, 2026. Our lead story: Pope Leo XIV left Rome's Gemelli Hospital on Saturday, several days after surgery for lung cancer. The operation removed the lower lobe of his right lung. He is scheduled to travel to Latin America in November. Also today. Violent clashes, looting and fires broke out across France after a day of cost of living protests. More than 1,200 people were arrested. In Canada, several people were dead or injured in a major fire at a military base in Alberta. Officials have not yet given a cause or a death toll. European diplomats were attacked by Israeli settlers in the West Bank. The Israeli military condemned the violence. Zelenskyy urged support for new US sanctions on Russia, after President Trump put them on hold. Now, a few notes by section. In Tech and AI, Anthropic is investing 100 million dollars to train 10,000 engineers. In Politics, Minnesota Senate candidates clashed over fraud, affordability and Trump administration policies in a debate. In World, hundreds of protests took place across France, and rescuers in Indonesia saved dozens of orangutans from wildfires. In Sports, Jasmine Jasudavicius won a unanimous decision over Erin Blanchfield at UFC Fight Night. The 49ers ruled out Nick Bosa for Monday's game. In Atlanta, Invest Atlanta approved a 330 million dollar bond for Amsterdam Walk. In Architecture, a Surat waterfront masterplan turns a neglected shoreline into public space. In Science and Nature, nearly 90 percent of countries have adopted biodiversity targets, but most remain off track, as the COP17 summit opens in Yerevan. That is the brief. Have a good day.",
